{"parentUuid":"0cd43fd4-8269-4bb9-ba8c-c88ba991acb5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"55f838da-35b9-4183-9a82-3286c8a3480f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F4eYZwuLz7j7wmczgudHjc","type":"tool_result","content":"26\t- **2026-09-21 FINAL: the Mac stays the GPS DB owner.** Eric briefly chose Windows (option A), then\n27\t  reversed the same afternoon: GPS, VALD and Perch pulls all live on the Mac. Nothing moved. The DB copy\n28\t  staged on Drive for the move was set aside in `FA2026/_Mark_for_Deletion/gps_db_handoff_2026-09-21`.\n29\t  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n30\t  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n31\t- 2026-09-21: **schedule moved to 10:00 and 16:30 daily** (was 06:30). Eric's choice. The Mac is awake\n32\t  at those times, so the asleep-at-06:30 failure and the `pmset` wake question are gone. Plist in\n33\t  `ops/` and `~/Library/LaunchAgents/` match; reloaded and `launchctl print` shows both triggers.\n34\t  First run under the new times: 2026-09-21 16:30 — check `gps_report/logs/last_run.json`.\n35\t- Done 2026-09-13, verified on Windows: the only task running `refresh_all_data.bat` is `\\Refresh_All_Data`\n36\t  (`_INBOX` copy, GPS step REM'd). No Windows task runs `bulk_import.py`. See\n37\t  `_INBOX/docs/handoffs/2026-09-13-windows-sync-refresh-task.md`.\n38\t- Checked 2026-09-16: scheduled runs 09-14 and 09-15 ran clean at 06:30. 09-16 failed (exit 4,\n39\t  NameResolution) because the Mac was asleep on battery; see Gotchas. Recovered the same day with\n40\t  `pull.sh` by hand: 2 imported (09-15, 09-16), 3 skipped, 0 errors, coach reports built.\n41\t- Optional follow-up: have `claude-stack-doctor` read `last_run.json` too.\n42\t\n43\t## Open questions\n44\t- Wake the Mac at 16:28 for the afternoon pulls? 2026-09-21: the Mac idle-slept at 15:45; GPS still ran\n45\t  at 16:32, but Perch and VALD started at 16:45 and finished 17:36-17:39 (Perch on attempt 3). All ok,\n46\t  no data lost. Fix: `sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 16:28:00`. Eric's call (needs sudo).\n47\t- Rotate the Catapult token (2026-09-21: Eric not concerned for now; parked) (plain text in `.env`, the CLI credentials, Drive `Bearer.txt`, and git"}]},"uuid":"6508cbc2-f24a-4c61-a8ba-8d75597744f8","timestamp":"2026-09-22T14:52:11.452Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md","content":"- **2026-09-21 FINAL: the Mac stays the GPS DB owner.** Eric briefly chose Windows (option A), then\n  reversed the same afternoon: GPS, VALD and Perch pulls all live on the Mac. Nothing moved. The DB copy\n  staged on Drive for the move was set aside in `FA2026/_Mark_for_Deletion/gps_db_handoff_2026-09-21`.\n  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n- 2026-09-21: **schedule moved to 10:00 and 16:30 daily** (was 06:30). Eric's choice. The Mac is awake\n  at those times, so the asleep-at-06:30 failure and the `pmset` wake question are gone. Plist in\n  `ops/` and `~/Library/LaunchAgents/` match; reloaded and `launchctl print` shows both triggers.\n  First run under the new times: 2026-09-21 16:30 — check `gps_report/logs/last_run.json`.\n- Done 2026-09-13, verified on Windows: the only task running `refresh_all_data.bat` is `\\Refresh_All_Data`\n  (`_INBOX` copy, GPS step REM'd). No Windows task runs `bulk_import.py`. See\n  `_INBOX/docs/handoffs/2026-09-13-windows-sync-refresh-task.md`.\n- Checked 2026-09-16: scheduled runs 09-14 and 09-15 ran clean at 06:30. 09-16 failed (exit 4,\n  NameResolution) because the Mac was asleep on battery; see Gotchas. Recovered the same day with\n  `pull.sh` by hand: 2 imported (09-15, 09-16), 3 skipped, 0 errors, coach reports built.\n- Optional follow-up: have `claude-stack-doctor` read `last_run.json` too.\n\n## Open questions\n- Wake the Mac at 16:28 for the afternoon pulls? 2026-09-21: the Mac idle-slept at 15:45; GPS still ran\n  at 16:32, but Perch and VALD started at 16:45 and finished 17:36-17:39 (Perch on attempt 3). All ok,\n  no data lost. Fix: `sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 16:28:00`. Eric's call (needs sudo).\n- Rotate the Catapult token (2026-09-21: Eric not concerned for now; parked) (plain text in `.env`, the CLI credentials, Drive `Bearer.txt`, and git","numLines":22,"startLine":26,"totalLines":61}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0cd43fd4-8269-4bb9-ba8c-c88ba991acb5","session_id":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"main"}
