{"parentUuid":"59b65ab5-8860-4d56-a9d9-1b9389badf5b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfJfdyoxrtoRLMF2meye4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UroRF2532DQoHrLfX1udtV","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md","old_string":"  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).","new_string":"  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n  2026-09-22: Eric believes the Windows writer is now stopped. Not verified from the Mac. If a GPS DB\n  ever turns up on Windows with newer sessions than the Mac's, the writer is back."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7737,"cache_read_input_tokens":86613,"output_tokens":1041,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7737,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1041,"cache_read_input_tokens":86613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7737,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7737},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01UroRF2532DQoHrLfX1udtV":{"file_path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md","old_string":"  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).","new_string":"  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n  2026-09-22: Eric believes the Windows writer is now stopped. Not verified from the Mac. If a GPS DB\n  ever turns up on Windows with newer sessions than the Mac's, the writer is back."}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfJfdyCzaDS828SFWkgxn","type":"assistant","uuid":"2a4e752b-bbb7-4755-af0b-fbfbd922ad13","timestamp":"2026-09-22T14:52:15.002Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"2a4e752b-bbb7-4755-af0b-fbfbd922ad13","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"55f838da-35b9-4183-9a82-3286c8a3480f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UroRF2532DQoHrLfX1udtV","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"5b2d053d-8380-4dda-8b3a-b87fc631732f","timestamp":"2026-09-22T14:52:15.100Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/DataBase_GPS_Reporting/docs/STATUS.md","oldString":"  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).","newString":"  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n  2026-09-22: Eric believes the Windows writer is now stopped. Not verified from the Mac. If a GPS DB\n  ever turns up on Windows with newer sessions than the Mac's, the writer is back.","originalFile":"# STATUS\n\n## Done\n- Repo brought under git and pushed to erash11 (2026-09-09).\n- 2026-09-13: GPS home decided (option A). This DuckDB is the one store; GD `FA2026/01_Raw_GPS`\n  is the raw mailbox. Import diagnosed: code + API work; the Windows `Refresh_All_Data` task\n  died silently since 2026-04-30 (likely `wmic` date step). Plan:\n  `docs/2026-09-13-regular-pull-plan.md`.\n\n- 2026-09-13: **regular-pull build** — Eric chose the Mac as DB owner, an automatic 06:30 launchd\n  pull plus manual `pull.sh`, and importing the mock game. Plan reviewed by Codex over 6 rounds\n  (APPROVED) and the code inspected by a fresh Codex session: `docs/2026-09-13-pull-build-PLAN.md`,\n  `docs/2026-09-13-pull-build-REVIEW-LOG.md`. `bulk_import.py --since-db`, receipts, exit codes,\n  atomic sessions, alerts, `ops/com.keystone.gpspull.plist`, macOS Chrome path for coach PDFs,\n  tests (`gps_report/tests`, `coach_report/tests`). `API_Token_FB.txt` and `*.pyc` untracked.\n\n- 2026-09-13: **pull is live.** Backup `gps_report/data/backups/gps_history_pre-backfill_2026-09-13.duckdb`\n  (SHA-256 match). Backfill `--start 2026-04-26 --end 2026-09-13`: 44 imported, 0 errors; DB 713 sessions,\n  newest 2026-09-12, mock game stored, no header without rows, all 44 listed sessions stored. Coach report\n  2026-09-12 built HTML + PDF. `pull.sh` by hand from `/tmp`: exit 0, 17 skipped, no alerts.\n  `com.keystone.gpspull` installed and bootstrapped (daily 06:30). Codex: plan APPROVED (round 6); code\n  inspected 3× (all REVISE, every finding fixed); the inspection-3 fixes and a later test-isolation fix are\n  not Codex-inspected (Eric's override).\n\n## Next\n- **2026-09-21 FINAL: the Mac stays the GPS DB owner.** Eric briefly chose Windows (option A), then\n  reversed the same afternoon: GPS, VALD and Perch pulls all live on the Mac. Nothing moved. The DB copy\n  staged on Drive for the move was set aside in `FA2026/_Mark_for_Deletion/gps_db_handoff_2026-09-21`.\n  Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find\n  and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).\n- 2026-09-21: **schedule moved to 10:00 and 16:30 daily** (was 06:30). Eric's choice. The Mac is awake\n  at those times, so the asleep-at-06:30 failure and the `pmset` wake question are gone. Plist in\n  `ops/` and `~/Library/LaunchAgents/` match; reloaded and `launchctl print` shows both triggers.\n  First run under the new times: 2026-09-21 16:30 — check `gps_report/logs/last_run.json`.\n- Done 2026-09-13, verified on Windows: the only task running `refresh_all_data.bat` is `\\Refresh_All_Data`\n  (`_INBOX` copy, GPS step REM'd). No Windows task runs `bulk_import.py`. See\n  `_INBOX/docs/handoffs/2026-09-13-windows-sync-refresh-task.md`.\n- Checked 2026-09-16: scheduled runs 09-14 and 09-15 ran clean at 06:30. 09-16 failed (exit 4,\n  NameResolution) because the Mac was asleep on battery; see Gotchas. Recovered the same day with\n  `pull.sh` by hand: 2 imported (09-15, 09-16), 3 skipped, 0 errors, coach reports built.\n- Optional follow-up: have `claude-stack-doctor` read `last_run.json` too.\n\n## Open questions\n- Wake the Mac at 16:28 for the afternoon pulls? 2026-09-21: the Mac idle-slept at 15:45; GPS still ran\n  at 16:32, but Perch and VALD started at 16:45 and finished 17:36-17:39 (Perch on attempt 3). All ok,\n  no data lost. Fix: `sudo pmset repeat wakeorpoweron MTWRFSU 16:28:00`. Eric's call (needs sudo).\n- Rotate the Catapult token (2026-09-21: Eric not concerned for now; parked) (plain text in `.env`, the CLI credentials, Drive `Bearer.txt`, and git\n  history `91a233b`)? Eric's call.\n- Rewrite git history to drop `API_Token_FB.txt`? Eric's call (repo is private).\n\n## Gotchas\n- **A NameResolution / \"Can't assign requested address\" error at 06:30 usually means the Mac was asleep,\n  not that Catapult or DNS is down.** On battery, launchd runs the missed 06:30 job during a 2-second\n  DarkWake (a brief background wake with no usable Wi-Fi). The process then freezes between wakes, and\n  the 2/4/8s retries all land in one dead window. 2026-09-16: started 06:48, failed 07:24, Wi-Fi\n  `E_CONNECTION_LOSS` at 07:07. Confirm with `pmset -g log | grep -E \"DarkWake|Sleep \"` around the run\n  time, then just rerun `pull.sh`. Do not lengthen the API client's backoff; it would freeze across\n  sleeps too and delay real-outage alerts.\n- A manual catch-up run also writes a `stale` alert line first (it checks the 36 h gap before importing).\n  That line is expected when recovering from a missed morning.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":28,"oldLines":6,"newStart":28,"newLines":8,"lines":["   staged on Drive for the move was set aside in `FA2026/_Mark_for_Deletion/gps_db_handoff_2026-09-21`.","   Eric reports GPS pulls also coming from Windows; 09-13 had verified the `.bat` GPS step REM'd, so find","   and stop that Windows writer next time on that box (two writers = two drifting DBs).","+  2026-09-22: Eric believes the Windows writer is now stopped. Not verified from the Mac. If a GPS DB","+  ever turns up on Windows with newer sessions than the Mac's, the writer is back."," - 2026-09-21: **schedule moved to 10:00 and 16:30 daily** (was 06:30). Eric's choice. The Mac is awake","   at those times, so the asleep-at-06:30 failure and the `pmset` wake question are gone. Plist in","   `ops/` and `~/Library/LaunchAgents/` match; reloaded and `launchctl print` shows both triggers."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2a4e752b-bbb7-4755-af0b-fbfbd922ad13","session_id":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"main"}
