{"parentUuid":"4e802778-a847-4faa-ac36-95ce03334a03","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfJfhSY8L8Ezxz2YcSRi5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cd29fcLweRkVKnhrfizvR6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler && ls; sed -n 1,40p ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_memory-compiler-pipeline.md","description":"Read memory-compiler notes before touching it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_read_input_tokens":103860,"output_tokens":355,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":189},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":355,"cache_read_input_tokens":103860,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Cd29fcLweRkVKnhrfizvR6":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler && ls; sed -n 1,40p ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/project_memory-compiler-pipeline.md","description":"Read memory-compiler notes before touching it"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfJfhRwugpKxJP2Xg9LRm","attributionSkill":"closeout","type":"assistant","uuid":"11852b71-d0b3-4a9d-81d2-f49ecbf0e5d2","timestamp":"2026-09-22T14:53:02.739Z","advisorModel":"claude-fable-5-1","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa3d84","version":"2.1.278","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"11852b71-d0b3-4a9d-81d2-f49ecbf0e5d2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c1cef4e9-555b-4c18-8126-f82f8653cbbe","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Cd29fcLweRkVKnhrfizvR6","type":"tool_result","content":"AGENTS.md\ndaily\ndocs\nhooks\nknowledge\nleftover-backup-2026-09-19\npyproject.toml\nREADME.md\nreports\nscripts\ntests\nuv.lock\n---\nname: memory-compiler-pipeline\ndescription: How the claude-memory-compiler flush/index pipeline fails and how to tell which stage broke; SessionStart injection was rewritten to a pointer 2026-08-29\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 174cde34-d23d-454b-8db8-9365e7f728f2\n  modified: 2026-08-29T20:05:21.521Z\n---\n\nThe compiler at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/` has three stages. Each fails\ndifferently and the symptoms look alike, so identify the stage before fixing.\n\n**Stage 1 — `hooks/session-end.py`.** Writes `scripts/session-flush-<uuid>-<YYYYMMDD>-<HHMMSS>.md`,\nthen spawns `flush.py`. Logs every firing to `scripts/flush.log` as `SessionEnd fired`.\nIf `flush.log` has no such line for days but the hook works when run by hand, sessions\nare being *closed* rather than exited cleanly — not a config break. Self-verifying: end\none session normally and re-check the tail.\n\n**Stage 2 — `scripts/flush.py`.** Calls the Agent SDK, appends to `daily/<date>.md`, writes\n`scripts/last-flush.json` **only on success**, and **deletes its context file on success**.\nTherefore **every leftover `session-flush-*.md` is a flush that died**, and its datestamp\nmaps to a missing `daily/<date>.md`. That is the cheapest diagnostic in the whole system —\ncount the leftovers. A stale `last-flush.json` means flushes are *dying*, not that the hook\nnever fired. Recover one by hand:\n`uv run --directory ~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler python scripts/flush.py <context-file> <session-id> [YYYY-MM-DD]`\nSuccess = `Result: FLUSH_OK` + `Flush complete` in `flush.log`.\n\n**The third arg is a backfill date, added 2026-08-29.** Without it `flush.py` always writes\nto *today's* log, so recovering old stranded files silently misfiles them under the current\ndate. Always pass the date parsed from the filename when backfilling; entries are then\nmarked `(backfilled …)`.\n\n**Batch-recovery trap — the 60-second dedup guard destroys data.** `flush.py` skips a run\nwhose `session_id` matches `last-flush.json` within 60s, and **deletes the context file on\nthat skip path too**. One session can have several stranded files (different timestamps), so\na loop that hits the same uuid twice inside a minute silently loses the second one — it still\nprints as consumed. Hit 2026-08-29: 12 files ran, 10 flushed, 2 dropped. Before trusting a\nbatch, check `grep -c \"Skipping duplicate flush\" flush.log`, and either group runs so repeats\nof a uuid are >60s apart or run repeats individually.\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"75199028-da69-4eb8-8040-4fb0e11ff74f","timestamp":"2026-09-22T14:53:02.931Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"AGENTS.md\ndaily\ndocs\nhooks\nknowledge\nleftover-backup-2026-09-19\npyproject.toml\nREADME.md\nreports\nscripts\ntests\nuv.lock\n---\nname: memory-compiler-pipeline\ndescription: How the claude-memory-compiler flush/index pipeline fails and how to tell which stage broke; SessionStart injection was rewritten to a pointer 2026-08-29\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 174cde34-d23d-454b-8db8-9365e7f728f2\n  modified: 2026-08-29T20:05:21.521Z\n---\n\nThe compiler at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/` has three stages. Each fails\ndifferently and the symptoms look alike, so identify the stage before fixing.\n\n**Stage 1 — `hooks/session-end.py`.** Writes `scripts/session-flush-<uuid>-<YYYYMMDD>-<HHMMSS>.md`,\nthen spawns `flush.py`. Logs every firing to `scripts/flush.log` as `SessionEnd fired`.\nIf `flush.log` has no such line for days but the hook works when run by hand, sessions\nare being *closed* rather than exited cleanly — not a config break. Self-verifying: end\none session normally and re-check the tail.\n\n**Stage 2 — `scripts/flush.py`.** Calls the Agent SDK, appends to `daily/<date>.md`, writes\n`scripts/last-flush.json` **only on success**, and **deletes its context file on success**.\nTherefore **every leftover `session-flush-*.md` is a flush that died**, and its datestamp\nmaps to a missing `daily/<date>.md`. That is the cheapest diagnostic in the whole system —\ncount the leftovers. A stale `last-flush.json` means flushes are *dying*, not that the hook\nnever fired. Recover one by hand:\n`uv run --directory ~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler python scripts/flush.py <context-file> <session-id> [YYYY-MM-DD]`\nSuccess = `Result: FLUSH_OK` + `Flush complete` in `flush.log`.\n\n**The third arg is a backfill date, added 2026-08-29.** Without it `flush.py` always writes\nto *today's* log, so recovering old stranded files silently misfiles them under the current\ndate. Always pass the date parsed from the filename when backfilling; entries are then\nmarked `(backfilled …)`.\n\n**Batch-recovery trap — the 60-second dedup guard destroys data.** `flush.py` skips a run\nwhose `session_id` matches `last-flush.json` within 60s, and **deletes the context file on\nthat skip path too**. One session can have several stranded files (different timestamps), so\na loop that hits the same uuid twice inside a minute silently loses the second one — it still\nprints as consumed. Hit 2026-08-29: 12 files ran, 10 flushed, 2 dropped. Before trusting a\nbatch, check `grep -c \"Skipping duplicate flush\" flush.log`, and either group runs so repeats\nof a uuid are >60s apart or run repeats individually.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"11852b71-d0b3-4a9d-81d2-f49ecbf0e5d2","session_id":"ecff9cb1-3f4e-4f95-becb-f41b76aa